{
  "protocolVersion": "chronicle-field-mixed-tomography-aggregate/v2",
  "claimBoundary": "Aggregate of independently recycled generic per-source-column shards. Each shard selects one empirically branch-activating intervention that rewrites exactly that supplied column, crosses it with every non-compound computational configuration axis the field-level workflow contract predicts can interact with the column, and adds a deterministic control sample of axes it predicts cannot. The eight conditionally active input-capability fields are explicitly owned by the configuration-space sourceSensitiveScientificCells campaign rather than silently listed as generic shards. Raw×source-sensitive sidecar rebind pairs are explicitly excluded and unestimated; that campaign proves only the generic LF-sidecar to CRLF-raw Parry rebind mechanism. Under every executed configuration every changed canonical output cell belongs to a declared output-cell family of that column, and no control axis introduces a family the base configuration did not move. Columns without an activating intervention in the checked catalog are outside this claim, and a declared family no configuration moved is recorded rather than asserted.",
